The rule for recovery says: "The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text" and "A candidate that parses as strict JSON, or as JSON with repeated keys resolved last-wins, is scoreable". For the input, the last object inside a code fence is the second fence's object B (with repeated keys), so the rule says recovery should return B. For the rewritten text, the added object C is after the fences, not inside any fence, so the last object inside a code fence is still B; the rule says recovery should remain B, unchanged. The code, however, does not apply last-wins to fenced candidates, so it skips B in the fenced pool, falls back to top-level objects, and in the rewritten text returns the later top-level object C. Thus the code moves when the rule says it should stay unchanged.